==Question #8==
{{Cquote2|People keep complaining about the wilderness being "dead". Why not move risk fights and pking that exist in pvp worlds back into the wilderness by removing pvp worlds?}}

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bpVigcSCZ0w&t=1807 Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Kirby:''' All that's going to happen if we do that is people are going to have their risk fights next to the Ferox Enclave and as soon as someone else shows up, "Oh, we go back inside now!". The problem is Wilderness... kind of needs to be dead? Because if the Wilderness was a hotbed for PKers, no one would go there, because it's full of PKers. Why would you go train your prayer at the Chaos Altar? You're just going to get PKed for all of your bones. It's a weird pseudo-state, it needs to have a low population for it to work, to have a population.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' Not sure if you're going to get many favourable responses that take...
* '''Mod Kirby:''' The Wilderness is bizarre. I understand it mechanically, but I don't know if it's good.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' It has a very interesting ecosystem, right? It is very delicate.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' In terms of moving PvP worlds, this is something that we have talked about before. The thing is, they've got quite an established base of players now that frequent PvP worlds, and having people accustomed to that - removing it, would be a bit detrimental, and could also be seen very similarly to Bounty Hunter, which we removed without really putting in a suitable replacement. So it currently serves a purpose.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' I think what I would rather see us spend our time on is bringing back Bounty Hunter, so that Edgeville becomes populated again. Then those that still want to play on PvP worlds can. What I imagine will happen is that if we brought Bounty Hunter back, PvP worlds would just slowly die off anyway as people prefer to go over to Bounty Hunter for whatever extra rewards you might be able to get from there. Then we could consider potentially closing them based on activity.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' Right now in its current format, I think it would be too risky to remove them and expect everyone to start fighting in the Wilderness again, especially when the player base is as small as it is. I think bracketing on PvP worlds helps you get fights more consistently. You have the option to be able to fight someone, plus/minus 10 or so levels within your range, just outside of a bank, as opposed to having to go 10 levels deep in the Wilderness. We would need to see some growth first before I think we could look at changing that, personally.
* '''Mod Tide:''' On the topic of PvP Worlds, what do you reckon it would be like if you could only enter the Wilderness on specific worlds?
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' It's also something that we've talked about before. In the original Wilderness changes blog, we said that we were going to look at limiting which worlds you could access the Wilderness on. It's one of the most popular suggestions from those that frequent the Wilderness anyway looking for players to kill, just because of how many worlds there are that you're required to hop around.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' I wouldn't say that we've completely ruled it out, but the feedback that we had when we first pitched that in the Wilderness changes was overwhelmingly negative to the point where it probably would be a detriment for us to do that straight away. Who knows, with different rewards in mind, with a little bit more of an ability for people to be able to fight back and incentives further for you to go into the Wilderness so it really feels like it's worth your time every time you're there, even if you get PK'd? We could consider something like that.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' I think that's what it would have to take before we looked at restricting the worlds - it giving you a really damn good reason to go there, knowing that you're going to get killed while you're there, and that being okay because it's not changing anything for you and the goals you're trying to hit. In its current status, I think it would just alienate a lot of players that are already feeling quite negative towards PKing generally.

