* '''Mod Ayiza:''' Maybe we look at taking the top people that qualify - we could split the 1v1s up to multiple 1v1 arenas and then take the top 10 people that won those 1v1s and invite them to an in-house tournament that's hosted at Jagex, for example. Something like that probably would be better. But I would love to see Dead Man continue. I think it's great!

==Question #12==
{{Cquote2|Has there been any discussion about expanding the places we can unlock the wilderness weapons? The rev caves are the only place you can get them and being a 1/20k drop while being risky isn't the greatest. Can we spread the three weapons across the 3 main wilderness bosses with a better drop rate so we have more options?}}

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bpVigcSCZ0w&t=2434s Youtube Time Stamp]

* '''Mod Kirby:''' To take this argument to its stupidest extension; "Twisted Bow being limited to CoX is stupid, can we have it dropped from goblins?" No. In terms of drop rates, we could look at it. Is it fine as it is? 1-in-20 is kind of ridiculous. I just looked at it and I was like "that is quite a lot for the three weapons..."
* '''Mod Tide:''' What about a Wilderness chest, like a really rare drop from there?
* '''Mod Bruno:''' I do think for the Wilderness weapons, that's kind of their charm. They're really rare drops from Revenants. So I don't really know how I feel about adding it to other places, especially if it's a common drop. The point is if you do really want those items, it's a bit of a grind. Those odds make it so that those items are pretty expensive. If you could just get the drops whilst you're farming out your Callisto pet or whatever, that would probably make it worth a reasonable amount less than what they are right now.
* '''Mod Kirby:''' It does look like it is 20k while skulled, by the way.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' It's 1-in-40k if you're unskulled... Well, you know what? Yeah, they're rare. I'm trying not to be sour this stream, I'm trying to be positive and uplifting, and not have negative takes. But this one for me, I'm sorry, is quite literally just a case of my personal take on it - We can, but we really shouldn't.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' As Kirby said, similar to CoX (maybe not with the goblin example, but it laid the foundations of getting the point across), those items come from those NPCs. If you want them, then you have to take that risk. Yeah, it's not the greatest, but that's the whole point of it, that's why they're there. And that's why those rewards have very specific niche uses within the Wilderness. If you don't want to do content within the Wilderness, you don't have to get those items! If you do want to do content in the Wilderness, you don't even have to get those items and you can still pretty much compete with the maximum rates - they're really just an extra bit of QoL onto it.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' So I don't like the idea of spreading them. It's the one charm that Revs have and if we were to remove those or put them elsewhere, then they've literally just lost their uniques. We already know how bloated that table is with rewards like alchables and supplies. So it's it's it's a no from me, I'm sorry. I wouldn't like that.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' The difference with something like the Dragon Pickaxe, because I'm sure that someone's going to counter it with "well that's hypocritical", is that the Dragon Pickaxe has a lot of uses outside of the Wilderness. Technically, if you look at statistically how long it takes you to get the Dragon Pickaxe and the amount of hours that you spend getting it, if you're on rate it only saves you like a minute amount of hours on the grind towards 99 mining. Then the only other use case for it being best-in-slot is for one encounter in Chambers of Xeric when you're against the Guardians - and you can do that just fine with a rune pickaxe!
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' So there's my counter for the "oh, I feel like I have to get it!" argument. But I understand players do want to get it because it does have general uses like around Gielinor, whereas those Wilderness weapons are very specific, their bonuses only activate within the Wilderness. I think the only use case for any of them outside of the Wilderness is for pure accounts as a replacement for the magic shortbow, because it's slightly higher damage output even outside of the wilderness. I guess the other added addition to the dragon pickaxe is the crystal pickaxe exists too...
* '''Mod Kirby:''' And the Infernal, yeah.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' So that's why, it's a little bit different. Just because that has a much wider appeal, it's one of those where okay, we get that, we can look at making it an option elsewhere. The last consideration is that we've already done it for the Dragon Sword, we did it for the Dragon Harpoon so we've made those tools accessible, especially the harpoon for skiller accounts that wouldn't have been able to get it beforehand because it was locked behind worms from Mount Karuulm. So there is a case for those that don't do combat that might want to unlock it that can't and, again, because of all the other factors, that's why we can consider it there. But for the for the rest of the weapons or rewards or items, for me personally it's a hard no.
* '''Mod Kirby:''' It just feels weird... Why do the Wilderness bosses have this pickaxe? It just doesn't thematically make sense to me. That's just my minor gripe as well.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' You have to remember the Wilderness bosses were added a long time ago. The community was very different back then. They were added around the same time where Old School was really in its first few years, and the majority of the community back then were PvPers because a lot of the PvP community fought to bring back Old School. So it was a very different dynamic.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' If you look back to the previous blogs that we put out in the early years of old school, they did talk about a lot of changes to the Wilderness and bringing in new content.The reception to that was overwhelmingly positive. People were giving us new suggestions, like "this would be really cool to see come from the Wilderness", etc, etc. Players wanted to go there to get those high value rewards. So looking at it, what would have made sense? The dragon two-hander, the dragon pickaxe, they had some new shields and that kind of stuff.
* '''Mod Ayiza:''' It's not so much the same nowadays. That's why it was added, it was just players wanted it at the time, and now they don't. Darn those ironmen... sorry, I love you ironmen, really!

